    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/director-of-admissions-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Director of Admissions",
      "description": "Director of Admissions - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Director of Admissions - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Director of Admissions Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Enrollment Management Admissions Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 5 2026 Closing on: Oct 18 2026 Title: Dir Admissions Employee Classification: AP - Administrative Professional Pay Grade: AP09 Division: Enrollment Management Subdivision: Adm Internal Oper Department: Enrollment Management Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Director of Admissions will play a critical role in overseeing the recruitment team and providing strategic direction for undergraduate and international admissions as well as orientation and onboarding programs. This role will also serve as a liaison with key stakeholders, including alumni, donors, faculty, staff, high school representatives, community college representatives, community based organizations and third-party vendors to ensure the university's admissions goals align with the institution's mission and values. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Develop and implement comprehensive enrollment strategies, aligning with the university's mission, to attract and enroll a diverse student population. Provide visionary leadership and strategic direction to the admissions team, ensuring the achievement of enrollment goals. Utilize data analysis to inform decision making, identify trends, develop effective recruitment and admissions strategies, measure performance against established goals, and rapidly adjust tactics when results are not meeting expectations. Prepare reports, presentations, and analyses of admissions and recruitment initiatives. Lead and supervise a team of admissions professionals, providing guidance, mentorship, and professional development opportunities. Set performance goals and expectations, conduct regular performance evaluations, and provide constructive feedback to enhance team performance. Coordinate and delegate responsibilities to ensure efficient workflow within the admissions department. Promote a culture of continuous improvement and innovation within the team. Oversee the admissions process, from initial inquiry to orientation and enrollment, ensuring a seamless and efficient experience for prospective students. Evaluate and enhance admissions and onboarding policies, procedures, and practices to optimize efficiency and effectiveness. Stay updated on the latest industry trends, best practices, and legal requirements related to admissions and enrollment. Collaborate with other departments, such as marketing, financial aid, housing, dining and academic advising, to streamline processes and improve the overall student experience. Build and maintain strong relationships with key stakeholders, including alumni, donors, faculty, staff, high school representatives, community college representatives, community based organizations and third-party vendors to support enrollment initiatives. Collaborate with faculty and academic departments to develop recruitment and onboarding strategies and initiatives that align with their program objectives. Serve as a university representative at various events, both on and off-campus, to promote Eastern Michigan University and its admissions process. Act as primary representative for the Vice President of Enrollment at internal and external meetings as needed. Minimum Qualifications: A bachelor's degree is required. A minimum of five years of progressive experience in college admissions is required. Proven experience in a leadership role within admissions, enrollment management, or a related field is required. Strong understanding of admissions processes, enrollment trends, and best practices in higher education. Proficiency in utilizing data analysis and CRM systems (preferably Slate) to inform decision making and drive recruitment strategies. Excellent interpersonal, communication, and presentation skills, with the ability to effectively engage with diverse audiences. Demonstrated ability to lead and motivate a team, fostering collaboration, appreciation, and a positive work culture. Knowledge of legal and ethical standards in higher education admissions including NCAA, Mid-American Conference, EMU policies, rules, regulations, and operational procedures. Ability to work independently, prioritize tasks, and meet deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Flexibility to adapt to changing needs and priorities within the enrollment landscape. Preferred Qualifications: A master's degree is preferred. Special Instructions: Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert b7417a34 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Enrollment Management Enrollment Management Categories Admissions Admissions First Name (required) ba1423f5 Last Name (required) 217f2cd3 Email (required) e91276c3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Title IX Investigator Chief Diversity Officer Reporting to the University Title IX Coordinator, the Title IX Investigator will be the university's lead internal investigator in cases involving complaints of sexual misconduct, sexual harassment, and gender-related discrimination or violence, including stalking and intimate partner violence. The primary responsibility for this po