    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/director-career-development-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Senior Director, Career Development",
      "description": "Senior Director, Career Development - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Senior Director, Career Development - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Senior Director, Career Development Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States EMU Foundation and Advancement Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Sep 16 2026 Closing on: Oct 16 2026 Title: Senior Director, Career Development Employee Classification: AP - Administrative Professional Pay Grade: AP 09 Division: Advancement Subdivision: Career Development Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Eastern Michigan University seeks a dynamic, innovative, and student-centered leader to serve as Senior Director, Career Development within the University Career Development Center. This position represents an exciting opportunity to help reimagine career development at Eastern Michigan University and strengthen the ways EMU prepares students to translate their education, experiences, talents, and aspirations into meaningful careers and lives. The successful candidate will understand that career development is not a single office, program, or moment near graduation. It is an essential part of the student experience and a shared University responsibility. This is a role for a builder, collaborator, and innovator who can help EMU think boldly about the future of career development while translating that vision into programs, partnerships, experiences, and measurable outcomes for students. The Sr. Director will be a transformative leader who brings an entrepreneurial mindset to career development. Working collaboratively across the University, this individual will help strengthen a career development ecosystem that begins early in the student experience, extends across academic disciplines, and connects students with industry employers, alumni, faculty, staff, and other partners. Reporting jointly to the Vice President for Advancement and the Assistant Vice President for Alumni Engagement, the Sr. Director will provide strategic and administrative leadership for career development programs, initiatives, partnerships, technology, communications, and outreach within the University Career Development Center. They will work closely with University partners to develop and implement innovative approaches to career exploration, career readiness, professional development, experiential learning, employer engagement, and student success. The will expand the reach and impact of career development across the University and ensure students have access to high-quality career resources, experiences, relationships, and opportunities. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Provide leadership for the development, implementation, assessment, and continuous improvement of career development programs and initiatives serving EMU students and alumni. Help develop and execute a comprehensive vision for career development that integrates career exploration and preparation throughout the student experience. Identify opportunities to innovate and expand programming in response to changing student needs, employer expectations, emerging technologies, economic conditions, and workforce trends. Build strong partnerships with academic colleges, departments, faculty, advisors, student-success professionals, alumni engagement, advancement, and other University units. Develop innovative strategies for engaging students earlier and more consistently in career exploration, professional development, experiential learning, networking, and career preparation. Partner with employers, alumni, community organizations, and industry leaders to create meaningful connections and opportunities for students. Expand opportunities for internships, experiential learning, mentoring, employer engagement, networking, and other experiences that prepare students for successful transitions from college to career. Develop and coordinate programs, workshops, events, resources, and other experiences that strengthen career readiness and professional competencies. Provide leadership and support for career fairs, employer engagement programs, networking opportunities, industry-focused events, alumni career programs, and other signature experiences. Develop strategies to ensure career development programs and resources are accessible and responsive to EMU's broad and diverse student population. Serve as a resource and representative of the Center and provide leadership on career development, partnerships, marketing, and outreach. Assist in developing and implementing marketing, communications, and outreach strategies that increase awareness and engagement. Collaborate on continuous improvement of the Center's website, digital resources, social media, communications, and other platforms. Explore and advance emerging technologies, including artificial intelligence and digital career platforms, to expand access, personalize the student experience, and prepare students for a changing workplace. Use data, assessment, student and employer feedback, and workforce trends to evaluate programs, demonstrate impact, and guide strategic decision-making. Develop meaningful measures of student engagement and career outcomes and contribute to a culture of assessment and continuous improvement. Assist with annual and periodic reports, career outcomes information, employment trend analyses, and other materials demonstrating impact. Assist with development and monitoring of the Center budget and strategic deployment of resources. Supervise, coach, and develop assigned professional, support, and student staff. Represent the Department at professional conferences, meetings, employer and community events, and on University committees. Maintain knowledge of national trends and emerging practices in career development, higher education, workforce development, experiential learning, and student success. Identify opportunities for partnerships, sponsorships, external resources, and collaborations that expand career development opportunities for EMU students. Adhere to applicable Eastern Michigan University policies, rules, regulations, and operational procedures. Perform related departmental duties, as required. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of higher education, career development, workforce and recruiting trends, experiential learning, communications and marketing strategies, employer engagement, and program development typically acquired through completion of a master's degree in Higher Education, College Student Personnel, Counseling, Human Resources, Business, Communications, Marketing, or a related field is required. At least five years of progressively responsible professional experience in career development, higher education, workforce development, employer relations, student success, experiential learning, or a closely related area is required. Demonstrated experience supervising, developing, or leading staff is required. The Director will lead a team of 6-8 career services professionals, with the opportunity to grow leadership in the future, both personally and within the team. Demonstrated ability to develop and implement programs, initiatives, or partnerships from concept through execution is required. Strong interpersonal, written, verbal, organizational, and collaborative leadership skills are required. Demonstrated ability to establish productive relationships with students, faculty, staff, administrators, employers, alumni, and external partners is required. Experience using technology, data, assessment, and feedback to improve programs, services, or constituent experiences is required. Preferred Qualifications: Direct experience in career services, career development, employer relations, experiential learning, workforce development, academic advising, or another student-success function in higher education is preferred. Experience developing innovative career programs, employer partnerships, experiential learning opportunities, or student engagement initiatives is preferred. Experience with career management platforms, CRM systems, digital engagement tools, artificial intelligence, or other emerging technologies relevant to career development is preferred. Special Instructions: This position may be filled at the Director or Senior Director levels. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert cf9b4ab5 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments EMU Foundation and Advancement EMU Foundation and Advancement Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) ccaa8f9d Last Name (required) 5f5c79fb Email (required) 39f78ab3 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Title IX Investigator Chief Diversity Officer Reporting to the University Title IX Coordinator, the Title IX Investigator will be the university's lead internal investigator in cases involving complaints of sexual misconduct, sexual harassment, and gender-related discrimination or violence, including stalking and intimate partner violence. The primary responsibility for this position is managing the daily responsibilities associated with incident investigations, as reported to and in close collaboration with the Title IX Coordinator. When a complaint is filed, the Title IX Investigator will conduct a prompt and thorough investigation in accordance with federal and 6th Circuit guidelines. The Title IX Investigator acts as a neutral party in the investigation and provides a detailed, unbiased report of the investigation's findings, in accordance with Title IX requirements. Assistant Director of Facilities Student Life This position will provide direct oversight of Rec/IM indoor and outdoor facilities. Coordinate all facility rentals/reservations to include; scheduling of all academic classes, Rec/IM programs, special events. Work collaboratively with professional staff to ensure all events are properly staffed, and invoices are distributed and paid in a timely manner, and all program needs are met from a facility perspective. This role will lead all risk management plans and assist in properly training Rec/IM staff and will also serve as second in command in the absence of the Director. Payment & Student Acct Spec Business and Finance Act as the primary point of contact for and have a working knowledge of all areas of Student Business Services, including Student Accounts, Departmental Processing, Collections, Third Party and Eagle Card. Perform cash handling related clerical and customer service activities in support of the department. Accts Payable Specialist Business and Finance Assist in the administration of diverse Accounts Payable transactions, including resolving complex issues. Work involves frequent internal and external contacts involving the daily processing of invoices and reimbursements. Although duties normally follow established procedures, responsibilities may include routine, minor corrections to facilitate processing. Graduate Assistant College of Arts and Sciences Provide support to the Department of Mathematics & Statistics. This includes tutoring in the Math tutoring lab and other duties supporting the mission of Eastern Michigan University. Responsible for tutoring, working with students on learning strategies, and other activities supporting student learning in the Department of Mathematics & Statistics. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 0e26ce3b Last Name (required) 218aad04 Email (required) fa11a190 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
