      "title": "Temporary Custodian (Pool)",
      "description": "Temporary Custodian (Pool) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Temporary Custodian (Pool) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Temporary Custodian (Pool) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Facilities Custodial, Operations, & Facilities Temporary Opening on: Jan 8 2025 Eastern Michigan University seeks to build a pool of qualified applicants for temporary custodial work. In this role, one will perform routine and heavy cleaning, and engage in upkeep of University buildings and facilities. Perform routine and heavy cleaning, and engage in upkeep of University buildings and facilities. Clean and maintain floor surfaces and stairways by sweeping, mop-ping, stripping, sealing, refinishing, and polishing, using hand and/or mechanical cleaning, scrubbing and buffing equipment. Clean mirrors, blackboards, interior glass and windows, drinking fountains, ceilings, walls, doors and other appliances and equipment. Vacuum and clean carpeted floors, stairways and upholstered furniture. Clean carpeted floors as needed. Clean lavatories and fixtures. Empty waste containers, ash trays and cigarette urns; and pick up refuse in buildings. Empty waste containers outside building entrances. Stock lavatories and other applicable rooms with necessary supplies such as soap, toilet paper and towels, and maintain an inventory of various supplies and equipment in accordance with specific instructions. Replace burned-out light bulbs. Clean, dust and polish items such as cases, ledges, furniture, equipment, fixtures, furnishings, venetian blinds and window casings. Remove snow and ice from building entrances, as directed. Move and arrange furniture, supplies, equipment and furnishings, as required, to perform assigned cleaning or to set up for various meetings and events. Maintain cleanliness of work and storage areas and all supplies and equipment used in the performance of duties. Report any damage, malfunction, irregularities and/or potential hazards in equipment or supplies to supervisor. Lock and unlock rooms and buildings. Perform related Departmental duties, as required. Minimum Qualifications: Ability to read, write, interpret instructions and perform basic arithmetic, typically acquired through the completion of a high school education, is necessary. Ability to perform physically active work of a medium-heavy nature, requiring frequent walking, climbing, pushing, pulling, stooping, kneeling and crouching activity to perform routine cleaning functions; and frequent lifting requiring the exertion of up to 50 pounds of force to lift a mop bucket, vacuum, ladder, or other supplies and equipment, is necessary. Ability to meet Departmental standards of reasonable personal hygiene is necessary. Knowledge of cleaning techniques and operation of custodial equipment is desirable. Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 12398728 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Categories Custodial, Operations, & Facilities Custodial, Operations, & Facilities First Name (required) 5dcb8cf9 Last Name (required) 2c949eec Email (required) 4241e4e2 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Institutional Research Analyst, Senior (IRIM) Inst Research and Accreditation Develop and maintain systems that enhance the utility of the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) data warehouse. Develop and maintain online and automated reporting facilities and interactive dashboards. Provide statistical support and enrollment forecasting. Collect and audit primary and secondary data sources to assure accuracy of data for analysis. Title IX Investigator Chief Diversity Officer Reporting to the University Title IX Coordinator, the Title IX Investigator will be the university's lead internal investigator in cases involving complaints of sexual misconduct, sexual harassment, and gender-related discrimination or violence, including stalking and intimate partner violence. The primary responsibility for this position is managing the daily responsibilities associated with incident investigations, as reported to and in close collaboration with the Title IX Coordinator. When a complaint is filed, the Title IX Investigator will conduct a prompt and thorough investigation in accordance with federal and 6th Circuit guidelines. The Title IX Investigator acts as a neutral party in the investigation and provides a detailed, unbiased report of the investigation's findings, in accordance with Title IX requirements. Assistant Director of Facilities Student Life This position will provide direct oversight of Rec/IM indoor and outdoor facilities. Coordinate all facility rentals/reservations to include; scheduling of all academic classes, Rec/IM programs, special events. Work collaboratively with professional staff to ensure all events are properly staffed, and invoices are distributed and paid in a timely manner, and all program needs are met from a facility perspective. This role will lead all risk management plans and assist in properly training Rec/IM staff and will also serve as second in command in the absence of the Director. Payment & Student Acct Spec Business and Finance Act as the primary point of contact for and have a working knowledge of all areas of Student Business Services, including Student Accounts, Departmental Processing, Collections, Third Party and Eagle Card. Perform cash handling related clerical and customer service activities in support of the department. Accts Payable Specialist Business and Finance Assist in the administration of diverse Accounts Payable transactions, including resolving complex issues. Work involves frequent internal and external contacts involving the daily processing of invoices and reimbursements. Although duties normally follow established procedures, responsibilities may include routine, minor corrections to facilitate processing. Graduate Assistant College of Arts and Sciences Provide support to the Department of Mathematics & Statistics. This includes tutoring in the Math tutoring lab and other duties supporting the mission of Eastern Michigan University. Responsible for tutoring, working with students on learning strategies, and other activities supporting student learning in the Department of Mathematics & Statistics. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 8d068379 Last Name (required) 99101fe4 Email (required) 35b087d7 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
