    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/director-of-prospect-development-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT",
      "description": "DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States EMU Foundation and Advancement Advancement Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 15 2026 Closing on: Nov 13 2026 Title: DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT Employee Classification: AP - Administrative Professional Pay Grade: AP 06 Division: Advancement Subdivision: VP Advancement Department: EMU Foundation and Advancement Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Director of Prospect Development provides strategic leadership for the University's prospect development program, encompassing prospect research, portfolio and pipeline management, prospect strategy, and advancement data analytics. Partnering with Advancement leadership, frontline fundraisers, and the President, the Director identifies and evaluates high-capacity prospects, optimizes donor portfolios, conducts confidential due diligence, and advances key institutional and volunteer pipelines. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Prospect Research and Strategy Lead proactive prospect identification and research aligned with University and campaign priorities. Analyze philanthropic capacity, engagement, and giving potential using wealth screening, data mining, and relationship mapping. Prepare actionable research briefings, profiles, and relationship intelligence for executive leadership and frontline fundraisers. Perform confidential due diligence on major donors, executive prospects, board candidates, and award nominees. Portfolio and Pipeline Management Oversee the prospect management program, collaborating with fundraisers to optimize active portfolios and pipelines. Facilitate regular portfolio reviews and strategy sessions to drive prospect movement across the fundraising cycle. Identify portfolio gaps, recommend strategic assignments/reassignments, and maintain data integrity within the CRM. Manage portfolio and fundraiser performance metrics, including maintaining and analyzing underlying data, calculating scores, facilitating fundraiser understanding and use of metrics, and reporting metrics to leadership. Executive, Organizational, and Leadership Strategy Serve as primary prospect strategist for principal-level prospects and manage the President’s prospect portfolio. Develop candidate pipelines for the Foundation Board of Trustees, Alumni Association Board, and other university committees. Collaborate with the Advancement Leadership Team on high-priority philanthropic initiatives. Maintain prospect development resources and training materials for Advancement staff. Alongside the AVP, develop projections for major and principal giving using data and insights from the CRM. Data, Systems, and Professional Responsibilities Serve as functional lead for prospect management data, partnering with Advancement Services to enhance reporting, tech tools, and workflows. Ensure strict confidentiality and adherence to ethical standards (e.g., APRA guidelines) in handling sensitive data. Participate in staff recruitment, team retreats, professional development, and cross-campus fundraising efforts. Stay up-to-date on prospect research and management tactics and strategies through self-directed professional reading, professional contacts, professional development courses, and training. Minimum Qualifications: Education: Bachelor’s degree from an accredited institution. Experience: 3-5+ years of progressive professional experience in prospect research, prospect management, advancement services, fundraising, or analytics. Core Competencies: Strong analytical, research, and communication skills; ability to translate complex data into strategy; sound judgment with confidential information; commitment to working effectively with diverse populations. Preferred Qualifications: 5-7+ years of relevant experience (preferably in higher education or a complex nonprofit). Proven experience supporting major/principal gift fundraising and advising senior executives. Hands-on experience with wealth screening tools (e.g., iWave, Windfall) and advancement CRMs (e.g., Blackbaud Raiser’s Edge). Professional involvement or training through APRA. Special Instructions: EMU is an Equal Opportunity/Affirmative Action Employer and Educator that is strongly committed to achieving excellence through cultural diversity. The University actively encourages applications from women, persons of color, and applicants with disabilities, veterans, and members of other underrepresented groups. Appointment Percentage: % Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert bacabb03 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments EMU Foundation and Advancement EMU Foundation and Advancement Categories Advancement Advancement First Name (required) 7954d086 Last Name (required) 7eb4d4ed Email (required) e2702b04 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT EMU Foundation and Advancement The Director of Prospect Development provides strategic leadership for the University's prospect development program, encompassing prospect research, portfolio and pipeline management, prospect strategy, and advancement data analytics. Partnering with Advancement leadership, frontline fundraisers, and the President, the Director identifies and evaluates high-capacity prospects, optimizes donor portfolios, conducts confidential due diligence, and advances key institutional and volunteer pipelines. Enrollment Advising Specialist College of Health and Human Serv Meet with prospective students, evaluate admissions applications, recruit at high schools, community colleges, along with other community organizations and prepa