    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/enrollment-advising-specialist-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Enrollment Advising Specialist",
      "description": "Enrollment Advising Specialist - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Enrollment Advising Specialist - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Enrollment Advising Specialist Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Health and Human Serv College of Health & Human Services Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 15 2026 Closing on: Oct 30 2026 Title: Enrollment Advising Specialist Employee Classification: PT Pay Grade: PT 08 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Health and Human Service Department: College of Health and Human Serv Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Meet with prospective students, evaluate admissions applications, recruit at high schools, community colleges, along with other community organizations and prepare reports on applicants, admissions and enrollments. Advise and counsel prospective students on curriculum requirements, vocational information, and academic achievement problems. Serve as a leader of the Admissions Strategic Recruitment Team, coordinating new and ongoing staff training and participating in every aspect of the overall recruitment effort for the University, including first year students, transfers and graduate students. Principal Duties and Responsibilities In collaboration with the Admissions leadership, lead the strategic recruiting efforts of the university by coordinating and participating in the overall efforts of the recruiting team. Represent the Admissions leadership, when required, in strategic recruiting conversations and analyses across campus. Assist in the development, implementation and assessment of strategic recruitment plans for all populations. Meet with prospective students and parents and inform them of University Admissions policies, procedures, academic programs, cost of attendance and all other matters related to choosing a college. Advise prospective students on courses, transfer of credits, curriculum requirements and other pertinent degree planning information. Provide advice to students on degree requirements, academic issues, and scholarships. Visit secondary schools and community colleges to meet with counseling and teaching staff, students, and administrators regarding Eastern Michigan University, and its features and benefits for college-bound students. Review Admissions applications and make admissions decisions. Make regular University presentations, on and off campus, to prospective students, parents and administrators. Represent EMU at recruitment fairs, graduate and undergraduate, around the state of Michigan and in other states, as required. Participate in all campus visit programs (on and off campus), as part of the overall recruitment effort. Administer Admissions policies and procedures for specific programs or activities. Advise clerical support and other professional staff on Admissions questions and problems. Recommend policy or procedural changes to improve efficiency and effectiveness in Admissions recruitment and/or enrollment practices. Participate in enrollment yield efforts (e.g., Fast Track, phone calls, e-mails, etc.) as required. Adhere to any and all NCAA, Mid-American Conference and Eastern Michigan University policies, rules, regulations, and operational procedures. Perform related departmental duties, as required. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge and skills in organization, administration, marketing, problem-solving and planning, typically acquired through the completion of a Bachelor's degree in a related field, are required. Two years of experience in an academic advising-related environment are required. Experience with transfer students and knowledge of the admissions cycle are required. Possession of a valid driver's license is required. Demonstrated ability to communicate effectively both orally and in writing is required. As required, ability to work evening and weekend hours, and travel, is required. Demonstrated ability to work as a part of and lead a team is required. Familiarity with computers and software programs is expected. Knowledge of EMU's academic programs, student type, undergraduate experiences and the southeastern Michigan area is preferred. Bilingual English/Spanish is preferred. Preferred Qualifications: Special Instructions: This position is fully in-person, not remote. The Expected starting salary for this position is $54,322 - $63,857 Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert c1144d03 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Health and Human Serv College of Health and Human Serv Categories College of Health & Human Services College of Health & Human Services First Name (required) d245536f Last Name (required) 7b06c1a8 Email (required) 9f5f7c7e Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT EMU Foundation and Advancement The Director of Prospect Development provides strategic leadership for the University's prospect development program, encompassing prospect research, portfolio and pipeline management, prospect strategy, and advancement data analytics. Partnering with Advancement leadership, frontline fundraisers, and the President, the Director identifies and evaluates high-capacity prospects, optimizes donor portfolios, conducts confidential due diligence, and advances key institutional and volunteer pipelines. Enrollment Advising Specialist College of Health and Human Serv Meet with prospective students, evaluate admissions applications, recruit at high schools, community colleges, along with other community organizations and prepare reports on applicants, admissions and enrollments. Advise and counsel prospective students on curriculum requirements, vocational information, and academic achievement problems. Serve as a leade