hree current references (no need for letters – contact information alone). Review will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. The Winter 2027 semester at EMU begins on January 11, 2027. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 8ee5499e Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts and Sciences College of Arts and Sciences Categories College of Arts & Sciences College of Arts & Sciences First Name (required) b39f17bb Last Name (required) 999bc19d Email (required) bd10616c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs DIRECTOR OF PROSPECT DEVELOPMENT EMU Foundation and Advancement The Director of Prospect Development provides strategic leadership for the University's prospect development program, encompassing prospect research, portfolio and pipeline management, prospect strategy, and advancement data analytics. Partnering with Advancement leadership, frontline fundraisers, and the President, the Director identifies and evaluates high-capacity prospects, optimizes donor portfolios, conducts confidential due diligence, and advances key institutional and volunteer pipelines. Enrollment Advising Specialist College of Health and Human Serv Meet with prospective students, evaluate admissions applications, recruit at high schools, community colleges, along with other community organizations and prepare reports on applicants, admissions and enrollments. Advise and counsel prospective students on curriculum requirements, vocational information, and academic achievement problems. Serve as a leader of the Admissions Strategic Recruitment Team, coordinating new and ongoing staff training and participating in every aspect of the overall recruitment effort for the University, including f