    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/public-safety-records-specialist-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Public Safety Records Specialist",
      "description": "Public Safety Records Specialist - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Public Safety Records Specialist - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Public Safety Records Specialist Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Public Safety Public Safety Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 26 2026 Closing on: Nov 16 2026 Title: Public Safety Records Specialist Employee Classification: CS - Clerical/Secretarial Pay Grade: 06 Division: Public Safety Subdivision: Public Safety Department: Public Safety Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Public Safety Records Specialist is responsible for the administration, maintenance, accuracy, security, and dissemination of law enforcement and public safety records in accordance with federal, state, and local laws, as well as university policies. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Performs complex administrative work involving police reports, criminal justice information systems (CJIS), records management, court documentation, and compliance with applicable federal, state, and local privacy and reporting requirements. Maintains electronic and physical filing systems, including documentation of all records requests and responses, coordinates and processes records requested by prosecutors, courts, attorneys, and law enforcement agencies and civilians using the guidelines set forth in the Michigan Freedom of Information Act (FOIA) and CJIS compliance. Assists with the collection, organization, maintenance, and reporting of information required under the Jeanne Clery Campus Safety Act, to include maintaining the Daily Crime Log and Clery Audit Trail. Performs records management duties, maintains compliance documentation, assists with the preparation of the Annual Security and Fire Safety Report (ASFSR), and supports the Clery Compliance Coordinator through accurate recordkeeping, data collection, and administrative coordination. Ensures proper document retention and destruction according to Michigan record retention schedules and university policy, while maintaining professional and confidential communications with all stakeholders. Support departmental administrative projects as assigned. Minimum Qualifications: A high school diploma or GED is required. Two years of administrative, records management, law enforcement, higher education, or compliance experience is required. Experience working with confidential records is required. Proficiency using Microsoft Office Suite, including Excel, Word, Outlook, and database software is required. Ability to learn applicable federal regulations, including the Jeanne Clery Act, is required. Preferred Qualifications: An associate degree in Criminal Justice, Public Administration, Business Administration, Records Management, or a related field is preferred. Experience working within a police department or campus public safety agency is preferred. Experience with Records Management Systems (RMS), Computer Aided Dispatch (CAD), or law enforcement databases is preferred. Knowledge of the Clery Act, FERPA, FOIA, and crime reporting standards is preferred. Experience preparing statistical reports and maintaining compliance documentation is preferred. Special Instructions: This is a full in-person position on EMU's main campus. The starting salary for this position is $49,130, or $23.62/hour. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert e6b89e65 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Public Safety Public Safety Categories Public Safety Public Safety First Name (required) ed8b2561 Last Name (required) 2518309b Email (required) 8f2bf796 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Public Safety Records Specialist Public Safety The Public Safety Records Specialist is responsible for the administration, maintenance, accuracy, security, and dissemination of law enforcement and public safety records in accordance with federal, state, and local laws, as well as university policies. Graduate Assistant College of Arts and Sciences Provide support to the Department of Computer Science. Accts Payable Specialist Business and Finance Assist in the administration of diverse Accounts Payable transactions, including resolving complex issues. Work involves frequent internal and external contacts involving the daily processing of invoices and reimbursements. Although duties normally follow established procedures, responsibilities may include routine, minor corrections to facilitate processing. Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design) College of Arts and Sciences Title: Part-Time Lecturer (Art) The School of Art & Design invites applications for Part-Time Lecturer positions in the undergraduate program. We are currently most in need of a new Part Time Lecturer to teach Art Education courses. Depending on the needs of the program, which vary in the regular Fall and Winter terms, we may seek new Part-Time Lecturers to teach non-majors courses in studio art and art appreciation, foundations courses in studio art, or art history courses. Qualifications: Applicants must possess a terminal degree in their field (MFA for studio art courses or PhD for Art History). Art Education candidates should have a minimum of a Masters in Art Ed with substantial art education professional experience and / or a PhD in Art Education. Appointments for each term are finalized by the School Director. HR Business Partner University Human Resources As a strategic partner, the HR Business Partner (HRBP) aligns business objectives with employees and management in designated divisions/departments. The HRBP serves as a consultant to management on Human Resource (HR)-related issues. The HRBP assesses and anticipates HR-related needs. Communicating needs proactively with our HR department and business management, the HRBP seeks to develop integrated solutions. The HRBP formulates partnerships across the HR function to deliver value-added service to management and employees that reflect the business objectives of the organization. The HRBP interacts with assigned units to maintain a level of business acumen about the units' financial position, culture, and competition. Part Time Lecturer (Accounting Finance & Info Services) College of Business The Department of Accounting, Finance, and Information Systems in the College of Business (COB) is seeking a new Part-Time Lecturer to teach undergraduate courses in the new Financial Planning and Wealth Management (FPWM) BBA program for winter 2027. Ready to Apply? First Name (required) 23191f84 Last Name (required) 81abaafb Email (required) d67b11fb Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Candidate Details × This website uses cookies. We use cookies to personalise content such as job recommendations, and to analyse our traffic. You consent to our cookies if you click \"I Accept\". If you click on \"I Do Not Accept\", then we will not use cookies but you may have a deteriorated user experience. You can change your settings by clicking on the Settings link on the top right of the device. I do not accept I accept Please choose the category/categories"
