      "title": "Graduate Assistant",
      "description": "Graduate Assistant - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Graduate Assistant - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Graduate Assistant Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs Graduate Assistant Opening on: Oct 23 2026 Closing on: Dec 18 2026 Title: Graduate Assistant - Department of Computer Science Employee Classification: GS Pay Grade: GS 0 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Computer Science Department: College of Arts and Sciences Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Provide support to the Department of Computer Science. Principal Duties and Responsibilities This includes tutoring in the Computer Science tutoring lab and other duties supporting the mission of Eastern Michigan University. Responsible for tutoring, working with students on learning strategies, and other activities supporting student learning in the Department of Computer Science. Minimum Qualifications A Bachelor's Degree is required. Application to (or enrollment in) the M.S. in Computer Science program is required. Enrollment in at least 6 graduate credits during the Winter 2026 semester in the Department of Computer Science is required. Ability to work 10 hours per week (50% graduate assistantship) or 20 hours per week (100% graduate assistantship) is required. Preferred Qualifications: Tutoring experience is helpful. Special Instructions: Review of applications will begin on November 15, 2026, and will continue until position is filled. In addition to providing a resume, applicants should provide names and contact information for two EMU Computer Science professors who will provide good recommendations for them. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 9939079b Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of option