    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/part-time-lecturer-art-design-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design)",
      "description": "Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Business Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Oct 21 2026 Closing on: Nov 13 2026 Title: Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design) Employee Classification: LL - Adjunct Lecturer Pay Grade: LL 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: School of Art and Design Department: College of Arts and Sciences Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The School of Art & Design invites applications for Part-Time Lecturer positions in the undergraduate program for Winter 2027. We are currently seeking addition instructors to teach Art Education and possibly Studio Art, Design, Art Appreciation and/or Simulation, Animation and Gaming. Depending on the needs of the program, which vary in the regular Fall and Winter terms, we may seek new Part-Time Lecturers to typically teach non-major courses in studio art and art appreciation, courses in studio art, and/or art history courses. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Teaching may include a number of particular obligations which employees are expected to fulfill, including but not limited to: meeting with students during and outside of assigned classes, assessing student work and performance, preparing syllabi and course materials, providing copies of syllabi and course materials to their supervisor on request, and assigning and submitting grades in accordance with established Eastern Michigan University schedules. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Applicants must possess, or be in the process of completing, a terminal degree in their field (MFA for studio art and design courses or PhD for Art History). For studio art courses, professional experience and teaching within higher education may be considered commensurate to a terminal degree. Preferred Qualifications: Prior teaching experience at the college level is strongly preferred. Special Instructions: Appointments for each term are finalized by the School Director, after consultation with the area faculty. Please submit a cover letter and resume. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert a1341fad Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Arts and Sciences College of Arts and Sciences Categories Academic & Student Affairs College of Business Academic & Student Affairs College of Business First Name (required) 086bad7e Last Name (required) 4b293009 Email (required) ed075718 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Public Safety Records Specialist Public Safety The Public Safety Records Specialist is responsible for the administration, maintenance, accuracy, security, and dissemination of law enforcement and public safety records in accordance with federal, state, and local laws, as well as university policies. Graduate Assistant College of Arts and Sciences Provide support to the Department of Computer Science. Accts Payable Specialist Business and Finance Assist in the administration of diverse Accounts Payable transactions, including resolving complex issues. Work involves frequent internal and external contacts involving the daily processing of invoices and reimbursements. Although duties normally follow established procedures, responsibilities may include routine, minor corrections to facilitate processing. Part Time Lecturer (Art & Design) College of Arts and Sciences Title: Part-Time Lecturer (Art) The School of Art & Design invites applications for Part-Time Lecturer positions in the undergraduate program. We are curre