    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/part-time-lecturer-bmmt-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states-5cb10cfd-9cf4-49b3-a86f-a9260214ab50": {
      "title": "Part-Time Lecturer (BMMT)",
      "description": "Part-Time Lecturer (BMMT) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Part-Time Lecturer (BMMT) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Part-Time Lecturer (BMMT) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Eng & Technology College of Engineering & Technology Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Oct 20 2026 Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Title: Part-Time Lecturer (BMMT) Employee Classification: LL - Adjunct Lecturer Pay Grade: LL 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: School of Tech Prof Services Mngmt Department: College of Eng & Technology Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The GameAbove College of Technology, School of Technology and Professional Services Management (STPSM) invites applications for a part-time lecturer position in the Business Management Marketing Technology Program. The appointment will start in the Winter 2027 semester. The successful applicant will teach an online asynchronous section of Personal Finance (BMMT250 and, depending on availability, other possible courses. Principal Duties and Responsibilities The primary professional responsibility of the Employee is teaching. Employees are expected to develop and maintain their professional skills in order to ensure high quality education for their students. Teaching may include a number of particular obligations which employees are expected to fulfill, including but not limited to: meeting with students during and outside of assigned classes, assessing student work and performance, preparing syllabi and course materials, providing copies of syllabi and course materials to their supervisor on request, and assigning and submitting grades in accordance with established Eastern Michigan University schedules. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum required qualifications include a Master of Science or Arts with a concentration in Business or a related area. In addition, the applicant should have current professional experience in Microsoft Office 365 software and a strong understanding of budgeting, consumer finance, and financial decision-making. Professional experience in business, management, marketing, finance, entrepreneurship, technology applications in business, or teaching related to the discipline. Preferred Qualifications: Experience using Microsoft 365 applications, including Excel, Word, PowerPoint, and related business technologies. Microsoft Office certifications or other relevant industry credentials. Knowledge of business analytics, data analysis, and decision-making tools. Strong instructional, facilitation, and student-engagement skills in an online environment. vAbility to create a supportive and interactive learning environment that promotes student participation, critical thinking, and problem-solving. Commitment to providing timely, constructive feedback that supports student success. Special Instructions: Application materials must include a letter of application and résumé. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 64ceb33a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments College of Eng & Technology College of Eng & Technology Categories College of Engineering & Technology College of Engineering & Technology First Name (required) 8c9f870b Last Name (required) e33ed0cd Email (required) 8d42df88 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Public Safety Records Specialist Public Safety The Public Safety Records Specialist is responsible for the administration, maintenance, accuracy, security, and dissemination of law enforcement and public safety records in accordance with federal, state, and local laws, as well as university policies. Graduate Assistant College of Arts and Sciences Provide support to the Departm