      "title": "Director Charter Schools Program",
      "description": "Director Charter Schools Program - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Director Charter Schools Program - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Director Charter Schools Program Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Academic Affairs Academic & Student Affairs Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 28 2026 Closing on: Nov 29 2026 Title: Dir Charter Schools Program Employee Classification: AP - Administrative Professional Pay Grade: AP 09 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: Charter Schools Department: Academic Affairs Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Administer the Charter Schools Program including identifying applicants, preparing applications, negotiating contracts, meeting with state and federal officials and providing oversight of chartered public school academies. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Direct all activities related to the Charter Schools Program. Meet with prospective applicants, assist in preparing applications. Review facilities, curriculum, personnel and financial plans. Participate as a member of the Charter Schools Review Committee. Assist in negotiating contracts with public school academies approved by the Eastern Michigan University Board of Regents. Establish and maintain relationships with local, state and federal officials. Attend state and national meetings and conferences related to charter schools. Provide advice and support to public school academies chartered by Eastern Michigan University. Monitor the curricular, personnel and financial affairs of each public school academy chartered by the University. Initiate annual or more frequent audits of each public school academy chartered by the University. Assist University officials with the receipt and disbursement of state aid payments as necessary. Prepare and recommend University policy regarding charter schools as needed. Serve as liaison with other state universities that have a charter school program. Develop and monitor the Charter Schools budget. Prepare state and federal reports as required. Prepare an annual evaluation of the program and recommend goals for the upcoming year. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Knowledge of teaching effectiveness, curriculum development, personnel management and educational facilities typically acquired through the completion of post-master degree level work in education or a related field is necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Five years of experience as a K-12 teacher is desirable. Four years of experience as a K-12 school administrator is desirable. Experience working with K-12 finance is desirable. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert c5aa9a5a Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Academic Affairs Academic Affairs Categories Academic & Student Affairs Academic & Student Affairs First Name (required) 71f727d0 Last Name (required) a997a537 Email (required) 8613daba Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. Director Charter Schools Program Academic Affairs Administer the Charter Schools Program including identifying applicants, preparing applications, negotiating contracts, meeting with state and federal officials and pr