    "https://careers.emich.edu/jobs/part-time-lecturer-performing-arts-ypsilanti-michigan-united-states": {
      "title": "Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts)",
      "description": "Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts) - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts) Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States College of Arts and Sciences Academic & Student Affairs College of Arts & Sciences Adjunct Lecturer Part Time Lecturer Opening on: Oct 29 2026 Closing on: Nov 18 2026 Title: Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts) Employee Classification: LL - Adjunct Lecturer Pay Grade: LL 00 Division: Academic and Student Affairs Subdivision: School of Comm, Media, Theater Arts Department: College of Arts and Sciences Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary The Eastern Michigan University School of Performing Arts invites applications for a Part-time Lecturer – Artist / Teacher of Flute. Principal Duties and Responsibilities The successful candidate will teach applied flute to undergraduate and graduate majors and minors in the studio. Additional duties include teaching the flute secondary instrument class (for music education majors), recruiting, and performing/teaching at various department events and with various faculty ensembles. Perform related departmental duties as required. Minimum Qualifications: Minimum qualifications include a Master of Music degree or equivalent (preferably in flute performance) and significant applied teaching experience. The successful candidate should have an established record as a professional performing artist. Preferred Qualifications: College or university teaching experience is preferred. Special Instructions: Interested candidates should upload a cover letter, curriculum vitae, and a list of three current references (no need for letters – contact information alone). In addition, please submit links to video and/or audio recordings of representative performances in contrasting style (no more than 20 minutes). Review will commence immediately and continue until the position is filled. The Winter 2027 semester at EMU begins on January 11, 2027. Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Content missing Similar Jobs Custodian Facilities Rackham Day Shift Monday-Friday 5:00 AM-1:30 PM Porter Day Shift Monday-Friday 5:00 AM-1:30 PM Salary $19.35/hr $40,248/yr Facilities Maintenance General Facilities Salary: FM 15, Step 1: $25.09 an hour/$52,188.86 annually Shift: Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 1:30 PM Location: Main Campus Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts) College of Arts and Sciences The Eastern Michigan University School of Performing Arts invites applications for a Part-time Lecturer – Artist / Teacher of Flute. The successful candidate will teach applied flute to a studio of undergraduate and graduate majors and minors. Additional duties include teaching the flute secondary instrument class (for music education majors), recruiting, and performing/teaching at various department events and with various faculty ensembles. Further consideration may be given to those with the ability to teach or assist in other academic areas as determined by candidate expertise. This part-time appointment (no benefits) will begin in Winter 2027 Director Charter Schools Program Academic Affairs Administer the Charter Schools Program including identifying applicants, preparing applications, negotiating contracts, meeting with state and federal officials and providing oversight of chartered public school academies. Data Systems Analyst, Senior-IRIM Inst Research and Accreditation Create and maintain a data warehouse environment capable of serving the needs of both the Institutional Research and Information Management (IRIM) Department and the campus. Serve as project leader for designated IRIM projects. Create internet-based user input and query interfaces for creating flexible, user-defined data marts from a data warehouse. Design and develop effective ways to boost data warehouse performance. Act as liaison between IRIM and IT technical staff. Part-Time Lecturer (BMMT) Co