      "description": "Custodian - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Custodian - Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Kiosk mode Custodian Ypsilanti, Michigan, United States Facilities Business & Finance Staff Full Time Opening on: Oct 29 2026 Closing on: Nov 12 2026 Title: Custodian Employee Classification: FM Pay Grade: FM 06* Division: Business and Finance Subdivision: Custodial Services Department: Facilities Campus Location: Main Campus General Summary Perform routine and heavy cleaning, and upkeep of University buildings and facilities. Principal Duties and Responsibilities Clean and maintain floor surfaces and stairways by sweeping, mop-ping, stripping, sealing, refinishing, and polishing, using hand and/or mechanical cleaning, scrubbing and buffing equipment. Clean mirrors, blackboards, interior glass and windows, drinking fountains, ceilings, walls, doors and other appliances and equipment. Vacuum and clean carpeted floors, stairways and upholstered furniture. Clean carpeted floors as needed. Clean lavatories and fixtures. Empty waste containers, ash trays and cigarette urns; and pick up refuse in buildings. Empty waste containers outside building entrances. Stock lavatories and other applicable rooms with necessary supplies such as soap, toilet paper and towels, and maintain an inventory of various supplies and equipment in accordance with specific instructions. Replace burned-out light bulbs. Clean, dust and polish items such as cases, ledges, furniture, equipment, fixtures, furnishings, venetian blinds and window casings. Remove snow and ice from building entrances, as directed. Move and arrange furniture, supplies, equipment and furnishings, as required, to perform assigned cleaning or to set up for various meetings and events. Maintain cleanliness of work and storage areas and all supplies and equipment used in the performance of duties. Report any damage, malfunction, irregularities and/or potential hazards in equipment or supplies to supervisor. Lock and unlock rooms and buildings. Perform related Departmental duties, as required. Minimum Qualifications: Ability to read, write, interpret instructions and perform basic arithmetic, typically acquired through the completion of a high school education, is necessary. Ability to perform physically active work of a medium-heavy nature, requiring frequent walking, climbing, pushing, pulling, stooping, kneeling and crouching activity to perform routine cleaning functions; and frequent lifting requiring the exertion of up to 50 pounds of force to lift a mop bucket, vacuum, ladder, or other supplies and equipment, is necessary. Ability to meet Departmental standards of reasonable personal hygiene is necessary. Preferred Qualifications: Knowledge of cleaning techniques and operation of custodial equipment is desirable. Special Instructions: Appointment Percentage: 100% Apply Now! Want to hear about jobs like this one? Job Alert 53f6c83c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Departments Facilities Facilities Categories Business & Finance Business & Finance First Name (required) 13c7a0c2 Last Name (required) f7b1fcad Email (required) a74e896c Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Similar Jobs Title IX Investigator Chief Diversity Officer Reporting to the University Title IX Coordinator, the Title IX Investigator will be the university's lead internal investigator in cases involving complaints of sexual misconduct, sexual harassment, and gender-related discrimination or violence, including stalking and intimate partner violence. The primary responsibility for this position is managing the daily responsibilities associated with incident investigations, as reported to and in close collaboration with the Title IX Coordinator. When a complaint is filed, the Title IX Investigator will conduct a prompt and thorough investigation in accordance with federal and 6th Circuit guidelines. The Title IX Investigator acts as a neutral party in the investigation and provides a detailed, unbiased report of the investigation's findings, in accordance with Title IX requirements. Chief of Police Exec Dir Pub Saf & Parking Public Safety Reporting to the President, the Chief of Police & Executive Director of Public Safety and Parking provides progressive leadership, open communication, and professional management of the University safety, security, and parking function for the benefit of the University's students, faculty, staff, visitors and the overall community. The Chief/Executive Director understands the University's needs, issues, and environment, and ensures that safety, security, and parking initiatives and day-to-day operations are aligned with the University's operations, processes, objectives and goals. The Chief/Executive Director plans, develops and directs public safety, security, traffic/parking control, parking operations, investigation, crime prevention and campus health and safety (OSHA compliance) functions programs and activities. They will serve as a member of the University's Executive Team and participate in the formulation/execution of strategic initiatives that impact the University at large. Custodian Facilities Rackham Day Shift Monday-Friday 5:00 AM-1:30 PM Porter Day Shift Monday-Friday 5:00 AM-1:30 PM Salary $19.35/hr $40,248/yr Facilities Maintenance General Facilities Salary: FM 15, Step 1: $25.09 an hour/$52,188.86 annually Shift: Monday through Friday, 5:00 AM to 1:30 PM Location: Main Campus Part Time Lecturer (Performing Arts) College of Arts and Sciences The Eastern Michigan University School of Performing Arts invites applications for a Part-time Lecturer – Artist / Teacher of Flute. The successful candidate will teach applied flute to a studio of undergraduate and graduate majors and minors. Additional duties include teachin